# WorthIt.gg - copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Read by pipeline/extract_claims.py:load_env(), which does os.environ.setdefault
# per line, so a real environment variable always wins over a value here.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY - required. Every model call in the pipeline uses it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREATE IT FROM CLOUD CONSOLE, NOT AI STUDIO. An `AQ.` key needs an explicit
# service-account binding, and AI Studio's key-creation flow omits it. The
# symptom is a well-formed key returning 401 UNAUTHENTICATED /
# ACCESS_TOKEN_TYPE_UNSUPPORTED on every auth form (x-goog-api-key, ?key=,
# Bearer) and on every SDK version - it looks like a bad key or a Vertex
# misroute and is neither. Fix: Cloud Console, with "Authenticate API calls
# through a service account" ticked. Do not re-debug this from the client side.
# (`AIza` standard keys are rejected outright from September 2026.)
#
# WHICH PROJECT IT DRAWS FROM, and why that matters.
# The free-tier ceiling is GenerateRequestsPerDayPerProjectPerModel - per
# PROJECT, per model. So anything else billing to the same project competes
# with a batch night for the same 500/day Flash-Lite pool, and an `AQ.` key
# does not self-describe its project, which means a checkout cannot answer
# "does this key share a project with something else?" on its own.
#
#   Console display name : "Review Summariser"
#   Confirmed by the owner, 2026-08-17: that is an earlier working name for
#   THIS project, not a separate project sharing the key. Nothing else draws
#   from its quota - it is single-purpose, so the 500/day Flash-Lite and 20/day
#   Flash ceilings in pipeline/live_quota.py belong to WorthIt.gg alone.
#
# Recorded as the console DISPLAY NAME because that is what was verified.
# A display name is mutable and not unique, unlike a project ID, so if the two
# ever disagree the console is right and this line is stale - but a stale name
# is still enough to recognise the project, which is what the 2026-08-13
# BACKLOG entry needed and could not get from a checkout.
GEMINI_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STEAMGRIDDB_API_KEY - optional. Cover-art tier 2 only (pipeline/art.py).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absent, tier 1 (Steam's own official art) and the legacy fallback still
# resolve, which is correct for ~97% of titles. TILES ONLY - a `grid` URL must
# never reach an OG image.
STEAMGRIDDB_API_KEY=
